Earlier releases
========================================================================

0.14.0-beta (2026-06-23)
- Added: Notifications folder — alerts QtC itself generates land in
  their own folder instead of the Inbox, and never count toward unread
  radio mail.
- Added: "Get categories from BBS..." in Settings -> Bulletins lists
  every category the BBS carries, with counts, to pick subscriptions
  from. A newly appeared category leaves a Notifications entry.
- Added: The first-visit bulletin cap depends on the transport — 2 per
  category over VARA HF, 3 over VARA FM and Telnet.
- Added: Character-set selector (Settings -> App) — UTF-8, CP437 or
  CP850, so DOS box-drawing bulletins display correctly.
- Added: Keyboard navigation and a shortcut cheat sheet (F1) — move
  between panes, switch views with F2 / F3 / F4, and act on messages
  with single keys or Ctrl shortcuts.
- Added: Stop button — stops a download in progress and returns the BBS
  to its command prompt.

0.13.2-beta (2026-05-24)
- Added: Mail-Call downloads new bulletins and sends the outbox without
  stopping to ask. Manual connects still show the selection dialog.
- Added: Mail-Call can only be turned on once your Home BBS has been
  visited by hand, so the first unattended session is not a full
  mailbox over RF.
- Added: The BBS List shows each entry's type in its own column, with
  the fields that don't apply to that transport marked as such.
- Added: VARA FM bandwidth — NARROW / WIDE in place of HF's 500 / 2300,
  in the BBS entry and on the toolbar.
- Fixed: The Address Book, the BBS List and the FM bandwidth boxes
  opened too narrow to show their contents.
- Fixed: The connection banner showed the FM bandwidth with a stray
  "BW" in front of it.

0.13.1-beta (2026-05-19)
- Fixed: New-user registration was skipped on BBSes whose name prompt
  ends in ">", leaving the new user at a command prompt the BBS did not
  expect.
- Fixed: Missing characters, ghost lines and duplicate text in the
  Terminal view. Two parts of QtC were reading the same connection at
  once; one reader now owns it, and a line split across radio frames is
  shown whole.

0.12.1-beta (2026-05-15)
- Fixed: YAPP downloads gave up mid-file on weak HF links. QtC now keeps
  waiting as long as data is still arriving.
- Fixed: Giving up on a YAPP transfer left the BBS sending the rest of
  the file into the terminal. QtC now cancels the transfer properly.
- Fixed: New-user registration sent QTH, ZIP and Home BBS as bare
  values, which the BBS rejected.
- Fixed: PTT failed silently when the serial port could not be opened.
  QtC now says so, and suggests another program may have the port.
- Changed: The PTT settings hint explains that only one program can use
  the serial port, and which port carries PTT on dual-port Digirigs.
- Changed: The PTT port is opened with flow control off, so the serial
  driver cannot toggle RTS / DTR on its own.

0.12.0-beta (2026-05-07)
